<p>English has one r. <b>ر</b> <i>re</i> is a light tap. <b>ڑ</b> <i>ṛe</i> is made further back: curl the tongue up, then let it flap forward as it comes down. The romanisation writes it ṛ. It never starts a word, and it changes meaning: <b>بڑا</b> <i>baṛā</i> means big, <b>برا</b> <i>burā</i> means bad.</p>
